infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title One resolved path vs two install paths
  desc Identity is keyed by path — same path shares one instance, two paths fork it
  compares
    - label One resolved path
      children
        - label One cache key
          desc require.cache is keyed by the resolved absolute path
        - label Evaluated once, reused
          desc First require runs the body; later requires return the same object
        - label A genuine singleton
          desc Forty requires share one pool, config, or EventEmitter
        - label instanceof holds
          desc One class object, one prototype across the whole app
    - label Two install paths
      children
        - label Two cache keys
          desc A nested copy resolves to a second absolute path
        - label Two module instances
          desc Each has its own exports and module-scoped state
        - label Split state, two buses
          desc Listeners on one are deaf to the other's emit
        - label instanceof returns false
          desc Different class objects, no error; ~2x bundle and RSS
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
